Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when freedesktop-sdk's Ghostscript can safely read compressed ROM ICC profiles with its external zlib-ng.
Subject: ghostscript: use bundled zlib for compressed ROM resources

With --with-local-zlib=no, converting even an RGB PDF to CMYK aborts in
zlib-ng's inflateEnd while Ghostscript reads a compressed built-in ICC
profile. Controlled builds of both Ghostscript 10.07.1 and 10.08.0
crash with external zlib-ng, but succeed with their bundled zlib.
Limit the change to Ghostscript; do not replace the image's libz.

Resolves: projectbluefin/dakota#1675

diff --git a/elements/components/ghostscript.bst b/elements/components/ghostscript.bst
--- a/elements/components/ghostscript.bst
+++ b/elements/components/ghostscript.bst
@@ -22,6 +22,6 @@ variables:
     --with-drivers=ALL
     --with-system-libtiff=yes
-    --with-local-zlib=no
+    --with-local-zlib=yes
 
 config:
   configure-commands:
